ices  as our understanding of this virus  continues to grow  so does our approach to fighting and  that's  true and new approaches to testing but  it's also true in our strategy around  contact tracing and i want to make an  announcement about that tonight  starting this week we are joining with  the county in a new digital contact  tracing program  introduced by our healthcare partner  health vanna this new initiative  sends patients their test results as  soon as they're processed  by our lab and if you test positive what  health fauna  now will give you the option of doing is  entering the names and the numbers  of people you recently came into contact  with so they can instantly  and anonymously get a text message  letting them know that you that they may  have been exposed to covet 19  and linking them with resources to  immediately get a free test  in the coming weeks we're going to make  it possible for them to also get a free  test by mail  so they don't even have to leave their  house in order to see  what their status is and remember as  always  when you get a call from a contact  tracer in the county  please answer it please finish their  questionnaire  this is the way that we will make sure  that we can quickly control  who has covert 19 and where it's  spreading  as we've seen from the start of this  this pandemic doesn't just threaten  lives  it threatens livelihoods so as we stay  focused on measures to protect lives and  the public health  we keep seeking ways to help our workers  our businesses  our renters families hit with  devastating force by the economic blow  of this crisis  and we didn't need another reminder of  how bad things were but today we got  that notice  when we got the latest jobs report  showing slowing growth and employment  hundreds of thousands of people leaving  the labor force altogether  and permanent layoffs on the rise  this affects people across our country  and the talks around a new federal  stimulus  have to get closed 